msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:462
msgid "Number of words shown in automatic excerpts on archives, search and category pages. The WordPress default is 55. Posts with manually written excerpts are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:467
msgid "Read More Button Text"
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:474
msgid "Ex: Continue Reading &rarr;"
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:475
msgid "Customizes the excerpt button text. Leave blank to use the theme default."
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:487
msgid "Enables support for Markdown syntax, allowing you to write articles natively (like GitHub or Docker Hub)."
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:492
msgid "Code Highlight"
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:499
msgid "Enables Syntax Highlight support, which colors programming codes. It is only loaded on posts for performance."
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:507
msgid "Enable Comments Globally"
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:514
msgid "Master switch that controls comments site-wide. When OFF, no comment form, list, count or Recent Comments widget appears on any post or page — regardless of per-post settings or the WordPress Discussion settings. Useful to quickly kill comments on the whole site (e.g. after migrating to Discourse, Disqus or another platform) without bulk-editing every post. When ON, normal WordPress behavior applies (each post can still be opened/closed individually). External comment plugins (WP-Discourse, Disqus, etc.) that override the comments template continue to work regardless of this toggle. <strong>Note:</strong> manually added widget blocks (e.g. a separate Heading \"Comments\" above the Recent Comments widget) may need to be removed manually in <em>Appearance → Widgets</em> to avoid orphaned titles."
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:519
msgid "Comment Accessibility"
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:526
msgid "Adds labels and autocomplete attributes to the comment form."
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:531
msgid "Comments Separator"
msgstr ""

#: inc/panel.php:538
msgid "Text between Author and Post (e.g., \"commented on post:\"). Leave <strong>empty</strong> for WP default or type <strong>&amp;nbsp;</strong> to hide."
msgstr ""

